{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1455963-accession-of-talents","id":1455963,"title":"Accession of Talents","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-01T15:41:34-07:00","id":1455963,"title":"Accession of Talents","content":"If you extrapolate the talents abilities to connect to the level of accession than a talents accession would be alone the being able to walk and or change the multiverse. One of the things I think many people are missing is we only have the equivalent of Adventure level Talents right now while in both Aeon and Aberrant we have both Psion and Novas starting on the path of accession. Trinity Core book PG 71 clearly demonstrates this.<br /> Character. Target<br /> Tier. Number<br /> Mundane. 8<br /> Talent. 8<br /> Psion. 8<br /> Proxy. 7<br /> Nova. 7<br /> Aberrant. 7 <br /> <br /> now we know that most of the Proxy\u2019s have been artificially advanced we can easily see that as a type (Psiad, Nova, or Talent) Advances closer to accession their Tier raises. At some point we would see both Talents and Psiads raise to the same power tier as Novas. I discount both Aberrants and Psion because their advancement is artificial and dead ends. We know that Nova accession is one of independent power and Psiad Accession is a collective racial group mind but with Talents abilities to access the multiverse I see accession as being a casting off of the ties to and single reality. Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6379-tytalan","name":"tytalan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T16:59:52-07:00","id":1455972,"title":"","content":"Not the most non-biased position here, but check my signature. Fists of Flux has an option to what you are after with a slightly different background.<br /> <br /> The general idea is to have a different kind of character representing a different setting material. I brought the idea of Talents as super skilled characters and expanded it to Martial Arts, but it can be easily expanded to magic an all other forms of \u201cscientific magic\u201d. The result is something that starts with Wuxia, goes to Naruto and MCU Doc Strange.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T17:15:17-07:00","id":1455975,"title":"","content":"This has reminded me of the Jet Lee movie &quot;The One&quot;.<br /> <br /> Consider this concept: A Talent who has gained the power to actively move between realities. Not just steer their passage with dramatic editing, but to shift long distances (for lack of a better word) along the spectrum of probabilities into worlds unlike the one they originate from.<br /> Now add in their discovering a way to join or link with OTHER VERSIONS of themself.<br /> In &quot;The One&quot; an evil version is doing this by killing every other version of himself, because the physical powers and abilities of a person increase the fewer iterations of them there are, and he believes he will become essentially a god if he is literally the only version of himself in the multi-verse.<br /> <br /> Probably Self-Murder isn't the path you'd want characters to take if they're supposed to be good guys, but some sort of meta-physical joining? Becoming a single inter-reality gestalt entity...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T07:22:06-07:00","id":1456008,"title":"","content":"For my druthers I would prefer that Talents primarily achieve greater power through Weird Science. From Time Machines, Dimensional Portals and other setting altering machines to Biohacking, Cybernetics and related self-altering routes to transcendence.<br /> <br /> Sure Novas and Psions have some really awesome powers, but Talents can pretty much replicate whatever they can observe if given time and resources. And in this setting, they have seen some pretty <i>weird </i>stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T10:55:02-07:00","id":1456016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1455963-accession-of-talents?p=1455975#post1455975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has reminded me of the Jet Lee movie &quot;The One&quot;.<br /> <br /> Consider this concept: A Talent who has gained the power to actively move between realities. Not just steer their passage with dramatic editing, but to shift long distances (for lack of a better word) along the spectrum of probabilities into worlds unlike the one they originate from.<br /> Now add in their discovering a way to join or link with OTHER VERSIONS of themself.<br /> In &quot;The One&quot; an evil version is doing this by killing every other version of himself, because the physical powers and abilities of a person increase the fewer iterations of them there are, and he believes he will become essentially a god if he is literally the only version of himself in the multi-verse.<br /> <br /> Probably Self-Murder isn't the path you'd want characters to take if they're supposed to be good guys, but some sort of meta-physical joining? Becoming a single inter-reality gestalt entity...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One of my ideas for talent ascension is that as the Talent becomes more powerful, they learn how to contact their other selves from alternative timelines. This ability allows them to share knowledge and inspiration points (in-game mechanics, the character gains temporary dots for skills, edges, and even gifts they don't have or increase the ones they already have) with their other versions, of course, they must agree in the first place and the favor goes both ways. I think it goes well with their theme.<br /> Apart from that, I was thinking that perhaps they could gain more control over their ability to manipulate probability, space, and time, but I'm not exactly sure how to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T12:27:30-07:00","id":1456026,"title":"","content":"Another option for Talents is allowing them to build supertech based in other splat powers. It would make them capable of some crazy power and keep them human in basically all aspects, like Tony Stark or a gadgeteer, mad scientist or similar char concepts.<br /> <br /> Also access to creating the wondrous items like the ones in In Media Res, Adventure! etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T07:25:01-07:00","id":1456071,"title":"","content":"If I had <i>my</i> druthers, an uber-Talent would be more like a Solar Exalt, with \u201cpowers\u201d that involve letting him do things with his skills that transcend the normal limits of reality: a ninja using Athletics to run across snow without leaving footprints, for example; or a marksman using Aim to \u201cbend\u201d the path of a bullet he fires so that it curves around an obstacle and hits the target on the other side. <br /> <br /> This sort of thing should <i>include</i> being able to amp up Super-Science to fully keep pace with the Powered tech that Novas and Psions exhibit; but it should neither be limited to that nor required to go that route. Indeed, that's \u201cmerely\u201d applying the notion of transcending a skill's normal limits to Science and Technology. <br /> <br /> But more generally, I wouldn't tie their \u201cupgrades\u201d to just one aspect of what makes a Talent a Talent. The above focuses on Talents as the \u201cmega-skilled\u201d, for lack of a better term: but Talents are about Skill, Luck, and Intension. An uber-Talent who focuses more on Luck might end up with something not unlike a hypothetical Probability Manipulation Psi Aptitude or Quantum Power (neither of which exist in \u00c6on or Aberrant, but both of which exist in the more general \u201csci-fi psionics\u201d and \u201csuperheroes\u201d genres). I could even see one of the more powerful applications of this being along the lines of the OP's \u201cSliders\u201d suggestion, where the power is less about bending the timeline in your favor and more about interacting with other timelines. And Max Mercer would be a (possibly unique) example of leveraging this aspect of Talents to deal with time travel phenomena rather than probability manipulation or cross-time shenanigans. <br /> <br /> And an uber-Talent who focuses on Intension \u2014 well, that's where my understanding of Talents is at its weakest; but if I get it, this should be not unlike the Mega-Attributes of Aberrant, but temporary: while a Nova has Mega-Stamina (for example) all the time, the uber-Talent only gets that sort of benefit when he's actively applying himself to something Stamina related. It should always be something to the effect of \u201cspend a point of Inspiration, and for the next action/scene/whatever, gain these Stamina-related benefits\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T16:07:04-07:00","id":1456091,"title":"","content":"What I personally did was linking the Uber Talent powers to skills and made them capable of gaining scale (Intention), use skill tricks more easily (Skill) or reduce the target number (Luck) when using the chosen skill.<br /> <br /> In my play tests it worked in a very interesting way, it required some discussion on what was the theme and how the characters really saw their powers, but in the end they were super capable martial artists that could bend reality and ecosystem the energy of other dimensions.<br /> <br /> leacing my modest y away, if you ignore the bad English, the ideas in my books are good\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T20:00:13-07:00","id":1456100,"title":"","content":"Yes, they are. And the English isn't all that bad, all things considered. My single biggest gripe in that regard is that <b>Tomes of Inspiration</b> uses \u201cRoute\u201d when it <i>should</i> use \u201cRote\u201d. My other gripe concerning <b>Tomes of Inspiration</b> is that it could have used an editor: for instance, Deep Inspiration doesn't make sense for the Inspired, and really should list a prerequisite of \u201cnot Inspired\u201d. The other two Mystic Edges make sense whether or not you're Inspired; in fact, I'd recommend reworking the wording of the first sentence for \u201cSensibility to Flux\u201d (which ought to be called \u201cSensitivity to Flux\u201d) from \u201cWhile not\u2026\u201d to \u201cEven if not\u2026\u201d. <br /> <br /> And I'd like to see one more book in that series: a combination of <b>Fists of Flux</b> and <b>Tomes of Inspiration</b> into one book, adding in material about Techniques involving Procedurals and Intrigue, downplaying (but not removing) the \u201cMartial Arts and Mystics\u201d tone*, including more worked examples of Techniques, Ro<s>u</s>tes, and Wondrous Items, and including some sample characters to demonstrate how it all fits together. I'd even be willing to serve as editor for the book, to clean up the spelling and grammar issues for you. My recommendation for the combined book's name would be \u201cExcelsior!\u201d<br /> <br /> In short, <i>Fists of Flux</i> is a good start; but it doesn't go far enough in its presentation. I'd rate it at four stars as written; but it has untapped potential that keeps it from being a truly outstanding product. And, of course, editing issues. But despite those issues, I really <i>like</i> it, and I want to see it fulfill its full potential. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">* perhaps by moving the stuff specifically about martial arts and mysticism to a chapter focusing on martial arts chronicles. That said, I'd also like to see a setting option that builds off of something from <b>Trinity Continuum: Adventure!</b>'s Setting Secrets: a world parallel to <b>Aberrant</b> where N-Day never happened, but Excelsiors started appearing instead.</span><br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> But getting back to the original topic, what tytalan was asking for could be done using <b>Fists of Flux</b>: build a Technique with the Transportation Effect and the Inter-dimensional Tag. It would only be available to those with the Flux Manipulation Intensional Gift (also introduced in <b>Fists of Flux</b> as something only accessable to Excelsiors, the book's name for uber-Talents), making it one example of what Excelsiors are capable of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T00:16:33-07:00","id":1456105,"title":"","content":"I actually think your missing my point. I love the ideals for more powerful Talents but Accession is about coming to the point that they leave this reality behind. A Nova with Quantum 10 ascends and leaves this reality for a higher plane. When enough members of a species have a Psi of 10 the collective species ascends as a group mind to a higher plane. My thoughts where that when a Talent reaches a Inspiration of 10 their ties to any one reality are broken and they walk the multiverse a unseen presence that guides the various realities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6379-tytalan","name":"tytalan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T02:17:53-07:00","id":1456111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tytalan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1455963-accession-of-talents?p=1456105#post1456105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think your missing my point. I love the ideals for more powerful Talents but Accession is about coming to the point that they leave this reality behind. A Nova with Quantum 10 ascends and leaves this reality for a higher plane. When enough members of a species have a Psi of 10 the collective species ascends as a group mind to a higher plane. My thoughts where that when a Talent reaches a Inspiration of 10 their ties to any one reality are broken and they walk the multiverse a unseen presence that guides the various realities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got really sad when the Devs said Psi never, ever goes above 7. :/<br /> I thought basically the same thing as you (concerning &quot;Psi 10&quot; for example), but sadly that's only our &quot;headcanon&quot;. :/<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T07:35:07-07:00","id":1456120,"title":"","content":"I am not sure about the \u201cPsi never going above 7\u201d I am quite sure there was a \u201cso far\u201d. As far as Aeon era goes, Psi 7 is the limit for human development, and possibly Doyen too, but other species have lower limits and there is nothing wrong with them, other than their limits being lower. Actually, human limit is on Psi 6, and it was absurdly hard to reach. Psions are engineered to reach 7, and that\u2019s all. In a couple thousand years maybe humans have learned how to go beyond that limit, and maybe even ascend beyond reality as psi users.<br /> <br /> Novas in the other hand seams to be able to reach the infinite scale of Q10, but it may have been artificially increased by N-Day event.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as I see, Inspiration 10 is far from being the final form of a Talent. I would say taking the one of the Facets to 10 would be the final evolution of Talents, but so far it\u2019s 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T07:57:16-07:00","id":1456121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1455963-accession-of-talents?p=1456120#post1456120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure about the \u201cPsi never going above 7\u201d I am quite sure there was a \u201cso far\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ian Watson said here that the max is 7. :/<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1455472-%C3%A6on-prometheus-unbound?p=1455620#post1455620\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1455472-%C3%A6on-prometheus-unbound?p=1455620#post1455620\"> [&AElig;on] Prometheus Unbound - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1455472-%C3%A6on-prometheus-unbound?p=1455620#post1455620\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1455472-%C3%A6on-prometheus-unbound?p=1455620#post1455620 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I believe is the next major Trinity product coming out, so what are people hoping for? I know I'm hoping for more psi-tech gadgets and maybe some looks at smaller </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T08:22:43-07:00","id":1456124,"title":"","content":"There's nothing currently &quot;missing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Currently can be used as \u201cso far\u201d, also he is talking about system, not ascension itself.<br /> <br /> The point is, Yara fore example ascended in to other level of reality as a group. It could be the case of everybody using the 7th dot of telepathy at same time, but I doubt it would be the case, they could have teleported away, but I really think they reached a a point they reached the \u201cnext dot\u201d and just used the power coletivelly.<br /> Maybe it\u2019s possible if you reach all aptitude\u2019s at 7dot\u2026 maybe it\u2019s the final 8th dot power, maybe it\u2019s reaching psi 8 or 9 or 10.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T10:07:05-07:00","id":1456537,"title":"","content":"A couple of things to consider Psi of 7 is the current hard limit but the proxy\u2019s haven\u2019t accessed and can\u2019t. Humanity is not ready to reach PSI of 10 and not going to anytime soon. We know that other races have gotten that high and accessed. Remember part of the reason for the orders and the proxy\u2019s is to prevent humanity from accessing the ideal is to lock humanity into a trap by artificially accelerating their PSI while putting a limit on its advancement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6379-tytalan","name":"tytalan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T17:57:52-07:00","id":1456845,"title":"","content":"Consider how Storypath works and look at it that way. Psi 7 is the limit. Nothing says ascended psi being get higher. But Psi 7 is Scale 1. What happens when a species has sufficient noetic enlightenment to reach Psi Scale 2?<br /> <br /> (Caveat: this comment isn\u2019t anything that is real or in development or being written about. Probably not even being thought about. It\u2019s just my musings.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T00:29:07-07:00","id":1456859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1455963-accession-of-talents?p=1456845#post1456845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider how Storypath works and look at it that way. Psi 7 is the limit. Nothing says ascended psi being get higher. But Psi 7 is Scale 1. What happens when a species has sufficient noetic enlightenment to reach Psi Scale 2?<br /> <br /> (Caveat: this comment isn\u2019t anything that is real or in development or being written about. Probably not even being thought about. It\u2019s just my musings.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a post-\u00c6on era problem, but Psi 8 is at least conceptually sound. Psi users are currently limited to Tier 3 (at Psi 6 &amp; 7), but a theoretical Tier 4 Psi user is an option. Might be Psi 9, rather than 8 but certainly an option.<br /> What we lack for this particular issue is definition. We don't have powers for that level or limitations. No Transformation penalties yet, for the ascending Psi user.<br /> <br /> Psi 7 is the limit for now in \u00c6on. Much like Psi 6 is the limit for Psiads. Surpassing that limit is conceptually possible in-universe but not without outside assistance and firmly within game plot/homebrew rules. Changing this is a tomorrow problem, for any potential post-\u00c6on era books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T02:45:07-07:00","id":1456864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1455963-accession-of-talents?p=1456859#post1456859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is a post-\u00c6on era problem, but Psi 8 is at least conceptually sound. Psi users are currently limited to Tier 3 (at Psi 6 &amp; 7), but a theoretical Tier 4 Psi user is an option. Might be Psi 9, rather than 8 but certainly an option.<br /> What we lack for this particular issue is definition. We don't have powers for that level or limitations. No Transformation penalties yet, for the ascending Psi user.<br /> <br /> Psi 7 is the limit for now in \u00c6on. Much like Psi 6 is the limit for Psiads. Surpassing that limit is conceptually possible in-universe but not without outside assistance and firmly within game plot/homebrew rules. Changing this is a tomorrow problem, for any potential post-\u00c6on era books.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't really know what you're arguing. Yes, it's *all* a tomorrow problem. Psi 7 is the limit. That's going to remain until it doesn't. Which may never happen. But if it does, what that looks like is unknown. <br /> <br /> But sure, going beyond Psi 7 in any form is &quot;firmly within game plot/homebrew rules&quot;. So is everything, so I don't understand what point you're making.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T23:18:28-07:00","id":1456935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1455963-accession-of-talents?p=1456120#post1456120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In a couple thousand years maybe humans have learned how to go beyond that limit, and maybe even ascend beyond reality as psi users.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you think about it, there's no particular reason to assume that's tied to a hypothetical Psi of 10. We know that noetically-capable species tend to transcend reality as we know it within about ten thousand years of developing space travel, and we know the Doyen tried and failed. But we don't know that the species that ascended had higher psi than the Doyen, and we don't know that the Doyen failed because they weren't noetically evolved enough. They may have just screwed it up*.<br /> <br /> Perhaps having a decent grasp of how noetic flux works (Shame the Qin had the Doyen screwing with their understanding) and time to research it leads most species to discover that their universe exists within a continuum of universes and that they can get outside this universe somehow. There may be multiple methods of doing so- perhaps some are technological, some purely noetic, some in between.<br /> <br /> *It seems totally in character for the Doyen that some of them would try and rig the ascension so that only they and their buddies made it while the rest got left behind. Perhaps several different cabals did so, and the aggregate result was two million years of wandering the universe as angry paranoid lightbulbs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26448,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","user":"Shalmaneser","date":". 08-16-2021, 02:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}